etail":"Live","state":"in","statusPrimary":"Live"},"displayPeriod":"1st"},"tiebreaker":[],"boxscoreMinutes":false,"commentaryCount":74,"commentaries":{"112020":{"id":"112020","team":{"id":"3","name":"South Africa","abbreviation":"SA"},"mediaId":0,"period":1,"preText":"","text":"beats him outside off. Full length. But nowhere near drivable. On a fifth stump line so he has to play. Bavuma does well for his part again, not following the seam movement away.","postText":"<b>2.30pm</b> There's still a drizzle on. The covers aren't going anywhere. More are coming on actually, says Gnasher from the ground. The fans, without any cricket to imbibe, have sought out a more conventional high with drinks in their hands. So how're y'all keeping yourselves busy during the rain break? Wrong answers only. \n\nOdinlass: \"I am studying Koine Greek.\" Uhhh τέλειο\n\n\"testing my new 9 iron with my tempered window\" Azza's not good when left to his own devices. \n\nMik: \"Checking out Hanoi old quarter from the corner of my eyewith the rain on the big screen! Go Scotty\"\n\nHugh: \"Wrong answers only? I'm studying for final matric exams which starts in a few days \"\n\nlunch is a cricket tragic and here's proof: \"I am happily and joyfully watching SOMe othER TYpE of SPorT\" \n\t\t\nJames: \"Praying to the Sun God Ra\" Could you ask them for a billion dollars for me, just like on the side? Thanks \n\nCharl: \"Half marathon done, get back ready to watch cricket on the couch, only for it to rain. \"\n\nVinod: \"Anyone remember how back in the day, we had to look at cricinfo's statsguru, before AI overview came if we wanted to see a stat\" Still won't be able to get gold like There have been 415 Test matches with at least 1200 Test wickets across both playing XIs, but none with a better combined average (24.43) or a better combined strike rate (46.26) than Australia and South Africa in the Gqeberha Test. (Sampath Bandarupalli making me look smart)\n\nOscar: \"how are the crowds looking? I know last test raised some attendance concerns \" It was better than the first Test, plenty of kids in as well. Shame we're having a stop-start day's play \n\nBhargav : \"Could Markram have done anything different, knowing it was Boland bowling ? And what about Bedingham\" Markram could've tried to hold himself back, maybe played a simple block instead of a drive on the up. But this is the guy who won SA a Test championship. He backed himself to get that ball away and questioning that could lead to problems too. The only thing is Markram was very judicious about when to go at and when to hold back and that ball from Boland definitely fell in the latter category. The fact that he tried to hit it was anomalous to the innings he was playing. Bedingham was just new batter nerves, wanting to feel bat on ball, which is why I think Ackerman has done really well so far. He's held his discipline, even if the runs haven't come. He's left well. He's charged at Boland to nullify his seam movement. He's doing okay. \n\n<b>2pm</b> The rain has picked up significantly now. Additional covers are protecting the square. This is not going to be a fun day.\n\nICYMI - Chris Woakes joined us on the latest episode of the <a href=\"https://www.cricinfo.com/story/switch-hit-spell-from-the-wizard-chris-woakes-1558743\">SWITCH HIT</b> podcast! Go have a listen! \n\nRaj: \"@Sam: Boland has played in matches regardless of conditions and also done well - practically the whole of last Ashes, and was also the reason Australia could beat Indian down under last time. Yes, he struggled in a Bazball game in England but not that bad to class him as good only in favourable conditions.\"\n\nJim: \"Agreed with @Raj, Boland originally brought in as he had a reputation as a bowler who could perform on flat decks (ie- The Junction Oval in the Sheffield Shield). In only 5 of his 20 Tests have they played 4 specialist seamers, and most of these have come recently (where his averaged has 'ballooned\"\n\n<b>1.53pm </b>Umpires are getting together again, wary of a drizzle that's coming down and poof, we're off. Another interruption \n\nSam : \"@Tom - had Boland not had the other 3 in front of him I don't doubt he'd still have a great record but it's worth remembering he almost exclusively plays in scenarios that suit him. he'd have certainly played more cricket with another team but would have played a lot more with a) less support around him and b) in less favourable conditions more regularly than he has\"\n\nMohamed: \"Team in trouble and Cummins just coming into the attack. its relentless\" <a href=\"/cricket-videos/sa-vs-aus-2nd-test-david-bedingham-you-get-through-six-balls-of-cummins-then-it-s-starc-1558778\">The players know it too</a>\n\nAayushman: \"Watched the pre-game presser from David Bedingham about how <a href=\"/story/sa-vs-aus-david-bedingham-looks-to-make-most-of-second-chance-after-down-year-1558764\">he told his friends</a> regarding the challenge of facing one world-class bowler after the other from Australia in the same innings. He will have a new tale to tell his friends after facing Scott Boland.\"","shortText":"Boland to Bavuma, no run","homeScore":"20/2","awayScore":"0","scoreValue":0,"sequence":101202,"boundary":false,"bowler":{"athlete":{"id":"446548","name":"Scott Boland","firstName":"Scott","lastName":"Boland","fullName":"Scott Michael Boland","displayName":"Scott Boland"},"team":{"id":"2","name":"Australia","abbreviation":"AUS"},"maidens":2,"balls":20,"wickets":2,"overs":3.2,"conceded":5},"otherBowler":{"athlete":{"id":"489889","name":"Pat Cummins","firstName":"Pat","lastName":"Cummins","fullName":"Patrick James Cummins","displayName":"Pat Cummins"},"team":{"id":"2","name":"Australia","abbreviation":"AUS"},"maidens":0,"balls":6,"wickets":0,"overs":1.0,"conceded":2},"batsman":{"athlete":{"id":"372116","name":"Temba Bavuma","firstName":"Temba","lastName":"Bavuma","fullName":"Temba Bavuma","displayName":"Temba Bavuma"},"team":{"id":"3","name":"So